# .Must() on stored E!T values (a local, a field, an element, a deref, an if and a match
# value, a global, a const, a capture, a linear payload) was an internal compiler error
# in lower (MKH-915). With an argument, Must on a field holding an error panics with it.
# Both profiles, both targets.
case ok
stdout muststored.out
case err
args err
stdout muststored.out
stderr muststored.err
exit 101
